      "body": "ACK  b3d77ea0275e56ad5aca442100b66789b5c08ec5\n\nThe dropped `confirmed_only=True` is fine.\n\nThe old call was `send_self_transfer(..., confirmed_only=True, utxo_to_spend=self.confutxo.pop(0))`.\n`confirmed_only` is only consulted inside `get_utxo()`, which is short-circuited whenever\n`utxo_to_spend=` is passed explicitly:\n\n```python\n# wallet.py\nutxo_to_spend = utxo_to_spend or self.get_utxo(confirmed_only=confirmed_only)\n```\nSince `utxo_to_spend `is always supplied here, `get_utxo()` never runs and `confirmed_only` was already a no-op. Confirmedness is instead guaranteed by construction: \n\n\nBenchmark result is almost identical to the OP\n master  - 68.87 s   \n This PR  25.37 s   \n",
      "user": {
        "login": "ismaelsadeeq",
        "id": 48946461,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTQ2NDYx",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48946461?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ismaelsadeeq",
